I come home after work.
It is March, but it is still very cold.
I open the front door and see Sabine in the hallway.
Her dog Bruno is also there.
"Hello Maya," says Sabine cheerfully.
I stroke the small dog.
"I need a warm winter coat," I say.
"My thin jacket from Mexico is not warm enough."
"You are only wearing a thin jacket," Sabine notes.
"Do you know a good clothes shop?"
"Yes, there is a large shop in the city centre," she answers.
"It is very good, because there is excellent winterwear there."
"You will definitely find a thick coat there."
"Are you looking for a dark coat or a colourful coat?"
"I am looking for a dark coat," I reply.
"I finally want to put on a real winter coat."
"I am going shopping on Saturday."
"Good luck," says Sabine, and she goes outside with Bruno.
I go into my flat.
A warm coat is a very good idea.
